    "wordCount": 1460,
    "thesisStatement": "While economic sanctions have become the primary non-kinetic coercive instrument of modern statecraft, their historical efficacy in altering core state behavior remains profoundly limited; instead, broad-spectrum unilateral sanctions frequently inflict disproportionate humanitarian devastation on civilian populations, catalyze sophisticated illicit evasion ecosystems, accelerate dedollarization, and fracture the global economic architecture.",
