      "   A. The Hayekian Vision: The denationalization of money and algorithmic scarcity as a hedge against inflationary fiat debasement",
      "   B. The Structural Trilemma of Blockchains: Security, scalability, and decentralization limits crippling mainstream medium-of-exchange utility",
      "   C. High Volatility, Speculative Mania, and Illicit Flows: The reality of crypto as high-beta speculative risk assets rather than stable stores of value",
      "   D. The Rise of Stablecoins: Tether (USDT) and Circle (USDC) dollarizing global crypto liquidity while introducing profound run-risk vulnerabilities",
      "III. The Sovereign Counter-Offensive: The Rise of Central Bank Digital Currencies (CBDCs)",
      "   A. Defining CBDCs: Sovereign digital fiat operating as direct liability of the central bank rather than a commercial bank deposit",
      "   B. Retail vs. Wholesale CBDCs: Consumer payment democratization versus cross-border institutional interbank settlement modernization",
      "   C. Global Pioneers: The Bahamas Sand Dollar, Nigeria's eNaira, the European Central Bank's Digital Euro, and the Federal Reserve's cautious posture",
      "   D. China's Digital Yuan (e-CNY): Comprehensive state-led deployment, domestic retail integration, and structural cross-border ambitions",
